  {
   "line": 4,
   "text": "So here's the mismatch. Analog frequencies live on a ruler that runs on forever. Digital tones live on half a circle, from zero to four thousand hertz. Copying means deciding where each mark of the ruler lands. Wrap it round and round, and five thousand lands on three thousand. That's aliasing. Or bend it on once, and squeeze.",
